2DA V1.0
*
# ethren: weapons held in both hands although DCC counts them one-handed (docs/rules/equipment.md: d20
# initiative, a shield allowed). Only the animation changes: wielded with nothing in the off hand they
# take the two-handed stances and attack files (G13's ready cycles, A2 A4 A6; the ITM's overhand,
# backhand and thrust weights still pick among them, so a thrust is A6); with a shield or an off-hand
# weapon the one-handed ones (G1, A1 A3 A5). The true two-handed weapons (the ITM's two-handed flag:
# d16 initiative, no shield) take the two-handed files anyway and are not listed.
# Rows: an item's 2-letter animation code (ITM 0x22, art/sprites/engine_rows.md), or an item resref,
# which wins over its code's row. HANDS 2: held in both hands; 1: one-handed (an item taken out of its
# code's row).
      HANDS
QS    2
SP    2
PF    2
SV    2
